WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.606
Week six.

00:00:01.656 --> 00:00:06.240
Managing a brand for social purpose, with Libby Hogson from UNICEF Australia.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.426
Her premise: brand building in a charity is just brand building.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:15.446
Over sixty thousand charities, one per four hundred and thirty nine Australians.

00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:19.161
Funding grows about three percent a year, but donors are falling.

00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:21.683
Fewer people, giving more.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.553
Then trust.

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:29.626
The Edelman Trust Barometer found sixty one percent of Australians hold grievances against institutions and the rich.

00:00:29.676 --> 00:00:33.214
Forty percent see hostile activism as legitimate.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.574
When people feel an institution isn't serving them, trust falls.

00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:42.194
Trust tracks brand performance, so the trust problem is the growth problem.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.713
Awareness was fuzzy too.

00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:47.154
Forty percent didn't know who UNICEF was,

00:00:47.204 --> 00:00:49.324
only twenty nine percent linked it to children,

00:00:49.374 --> 00:00:51.842
and many didn't know it was a charity.

00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:54.983
About ninety five percent of spend went on conversion and retention,

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.073
and only five percent on awareness.

00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:01.331
They were optimising a funnel with an empty top.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:05.592
By 2020, UNICEF had zero unprompted awareness.

00:01:05.642 --> 00:01:08.386
Asked to name a charity, people never said it.

00:01:08.436 --> 00:01:11.287
Shown the name, they recognised it.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.377
That gap matters.

00:01:13.427 --> 00:01:17.268
People with UNICEF top of mind showed nineteen percent donation intent.

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:20.358
Aware only when prompted, just seven percent.

00:01:20.408 --> 00:01:23.582
Mental availability nearly triples intent.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.186
So which facts to lead with?

00:01:26.236 --> 00:01:29.158
Saves more lives than any other organisation.

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:32.165
The world's largest organisation for children's rights.

00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:34.817
Brings lifesaving help to children.

00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:40.801
Then came a polycrisis: bushfires, the pandemic, Ukraine, all at once.

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:44.374
UNICEF USA's version was too chest-beating for Australia.

00:01:44.424 --> 00:01:46.899
Positioning has to fit the moment.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.600
The positioning:

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.399
UNICEF inspires Australians with the determination it takes to protect and care for every child,

00:01:53.449 --> 00:01:54.508
no matter what.

00:01:54.558 --> 00:01:56.998
Determination is the key word.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.582
The proof:

00:01:58.632 --> 00:02:00.787
on the ground in over a hundred and ninety countries,

00:02:00.837 --> 00:02:02.391
help within forty eight hours,

00:02:02.441 --> 00:02:04.454
and one hundred percent donor funded.

00:02:04.504 --> 00:02:06.930
The message: Always there.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:09.706
Consistency isn't how you look.

00:02:09.756 --> 00:02:11.817
It's the place you hold in people's minds:

00:02:11.867 --> 00:02:12.701
one message,

00:02:12.751 --> 00:02:13.927
again and again,

00:02:13.977 --> 00:02:16.767
until you're sick of it and the public remembers.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.978
Earned media was key, with ambassadors matched to the moment.

00:02:21.028 --> 00:02:22.901
From 2020 to 2024,

00:02:22.951 --> 00:02:26.037
broadcast share of voice rose from twenty to fifty five percent,

00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:29.073
and news mentions rose two hundred and seventy percent.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.052
It was a whole of organisation job.

00:02:32.102 --> 00:02:34.505
The team moved from generalists to experts,

00:02:34.555 --> 00:02:38.325
and scrapped the digital marketing team so everyone could do digital.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.056
Did it work?

00:02:40.106 --> 00:02:43.028
Ad awareness and share of voice lift unprompted awareness,

00:02:43.078 --> 00:02:44.301
then donation intent,

00:02:44.351 --> 00:02:45.516
then market share.

00:02:45.566 --> 00:02:48.815
Top of mind tracked alongside revenue growth.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.408
After 2024 metrics dipped,

00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:52.905
but there's no tired brand,

00:02:52.955 --> 00:02:53.755
just a bored brand manager.

00:02:53.203 --> 00:02:56.714
Always there became Let's be there.

00:02:56.764 --> 00:03:00.482
And climate change fits, because it's changing childhood.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.060
The lessons:

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.794
it's a whole of organisation task,

00:03:03.844 --> 00:03:04.867
stay the course,

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:05.940
measure everything,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.202
skilled people matter,

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:09.442
and trust the data but still take risks.

00:03:09.492 --> 00:03:11.285
That's week six.
